{"parentUuid":"9c9c16a9-a5b6-4a70-a539-64a54c7dc116","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa4ed8539bae4b1e7","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HxK97VgV1DkrPbEf5bQHdV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI found the **ScreenLayout** component at `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/cloakanddagger/src/shared/components/screen-layout/ScreenLayout.tsx`.\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**ScreenLayout does NOT use React Native Modal component.** Instead:\n\n1. **The `type=\"modal\"` prop controls padding only:**\n   - When `type=\"modal\"`, it sets `paddingTop: 24` (fixed)\n   - When `type=\"screen\"` (default), it uses the safe area inset top value: `insets.top`\n   - This is because modal screens are offset from the device edge and need a smaller top inset\n\n2. **Visual indicator for modals:**\n   - When `type=\"modal\"`, it renders a visual drag handle (white bar) at the top:\n     - A semi-transparent white block (88px wide, 4px tall) with rounded corners\n     - Positioned with 12px top padding and 40px bottom padding\n\n3. **No orientation configuration:**\n   - The component does NOT set any screen orientations or `supportedOrientations`\n   - It wraps a `Screen` component from `@prototyp/skeletor` library\n   - Both `hideBottomSafeArea` and `hideTopSafeArea` are always set to true\n\n4. **Usage:**\n   - Found 16+ screens using `type=\"modal\"` including SetUpRecoveryKey, BlockedUsers, InvitePeople, StartChat, CreateRoom, VerifyPin, and others\n\nThe component is purely presentational for padding and visual styling differences between modal and regular screens—it does not handle native modal presentation or orientation restrictions at this level."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":22064,"output_tokens":398,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standar